{"id":"u-32d9c919-3a91-45a6-8b05-8580f52299a9","src":"community","title":"Dad's Return: A 4 week home gym return!","author":"Tr K.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/GZMLbP-4-week-return","desc":"The purpose is to knock the rust off and get the machine moving again. This 3 day a week program is made with the family life and those with a home gym in mind. (You can easily do this at the gym too. The key is to just start going.) If you have taken a serious amount of time off and want to get back into it, this will help wake up the muscles while limiting the chance of tendon injury (lets not get taken out before we even start). \nWeek 1.\nWarm up and for your working sets you are shooting for 5 reps in reserve. Nothing is done to failure but should still stimulate your muscles / pump.\nWeek 2.\nStill shooting for 5 Reps in reserve while staying in the working range. you may need to add weight if week one felt easy.\nWeek 3.\nWorking to a 4-5 Rep in reserve. Add weight if at the top end of rep range from last week.\nWeek 4.\nGood Job almost done with priming the machine. We are shooting for a 4 rep in reserve weight while staying in the rep ranges. \n\n*Rest Between Sets should be around 60-120 sec.\n\nYou can add 20-30 min low impact cardio between each lifting day walking, easy jog, stairs ect. This will help from skipping days and build a routine! \n\nWe all need to start somewhere and remember to just start. I hope this well help for those who like me felt overwhelmed and \"will just do it tomorrow\".  The change wont happen if you don't start!","level":["Novice","Beginner"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":50,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-17T20:57:32.295Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{